{
  "title": "Miscellaneous Aamal for the Month of Rajab",
  "data": "Dua Ya Man Arjuhu\nEach day in Rajab - in the morning, in the evening and after each obligatory prayer - recite:\nيَا مَنْ اَرْجُوْهُ لِكُلِّ خَيْرٍ\nYAA MAN ARJOOHO LE KULLE KHAYRIN \nO He from whom I hope for every good,\nوَآمَنُ سَخَطَهٗ عِنْدَ كُلِّ شَرٍّ\nWA AAMANO SAKHATAHU I’NDA KULLE SHARRIN \nAnd in whom I seek safety from His wrath at every evil.\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ الْكَثِيْرَ بِالْقَلِيْلِ\nYAA MAN YO’TIL KASEERAA BILQALEELE \nO He who gives much in return for very little (deeds),\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ مَنْ سَاَلَهٗ\nYAA MAN YO’TEE MAN SA-A’LAHU \nO He who gives to those who ask Him,\nيَا مَنْ يُعْطِيْ مَنْ لَمْ يَسْاَلْهٗ وَمَنْ لَمْ يَعْرِفْهُ\nYAA MAN YO’TEE MAN LAM YAS-A’LHO WA MAN LAM YA’RIFHO\nO He who gives to those who do not ask Him and those who do not know Him,\nتَحَنُّنًا مِنْهُ وَرَحْمَةً\nTAHANNONAN MINHO WA RAHMATAN \nOut of His affection and mercy.\nاَعْطِنِيْ بِمَسْاَلَتِيْ اِيَّاكَ\nAA’-TENEE BE-MASALATEE IYYAKA \nGrant me, by my asking of You, \nجَمِيْعَ خَيْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَجَمِيْعَ خَيْرِ الْآخِرَةِ\nJAMEE-A’ KHAYRID DUNYAA WA JAMEE-A’ KHAYRIL AAKHERATE \nall the good of this world, and all the good of the Hereafter.\nوَاصْرِفْ عَنِّيْ بِمَسْاَلَتِيْ اِيَّاكَ\nWAS RIF A’NNI BE MAS-ALATEE IYYAAKA \nAnd avert from me, by my asking of You,\nجَمِيْعَ شَرِّ الدُّنْيَا وَشَرِّ الْآخِرَةِ\nJAMEE-A’ SHARRID DUNYAA WA SHARRIL AAKHERATE \nAll the evil of this world and the evil of the Hereafter.\nفَاِنَّهٗ غَيْرُ مَنْقُوْصٍ مَا اَعْطَيْتَ\nFA-INNAHU GHAYRO MANQOOSIN MA A-A’TAYTA \nFor indeed, whatever You give is never diminishing (from Your treasures),\nوَزِدْنِي مِنْ فَضْلِكَ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nWA ZIDNEE MIN FAZLEKA YAA KAREEMO.\nAnd increase for me from Your bounty, O Most Generous.\nWhile saying this, grasp your beard with your left hand and keep moving the forefinger of your right hand. Then add:\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME \nO Possessor of Majesty and Honor,\nيَا ذَا النَّعْمَاءِ وَالْجُوْدِ\nYAA ZAN NA’MAA-E WAL JOODE \nO Possessor of Blessings and Generosity,\nيَا ذَا الْمَنِّ وَالطَّوْلِ\nYAA ZAL MANNE WAT TAWLE \nO Possessor of Favor and Bounty,\nحَرِّمْ شَيْبَتِيْ عَلَى النَّارِ\nHARRIM SHAYBATEE A’LAN NAAR.\nForbid my white beard (my aged self) from the Fire.",
  "tabs": [
    "Istighfar & La Ilaha Illallah\nIn Rajab, repeat 100 times and give alms immediately after it, or repeat 400 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِيْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA\nI implore the forgiveness of Allah. There is no god save Him,\nوَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nWAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nalone, having no partner, and I repent before Him.\nRepeat this litany 1,000 times in Rajab:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAH.\nThere is no god save Allah.\nEach morning and each evening in Rajab, repeat 70 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHA WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI implore the forgiveness of Allah and I repent to Him.\nAfter the 70 repetitions, raise your hands toward the sky and say:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِيْ وَتُبْ عَلَيَّ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LEE WA TUB A’LAYYA.\nO Allah, (please do) forgive me and accept my repentance.\nRepeat 1,000 times in Rajab, so that Almighty Allah will forgive you:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAH ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME\nI implore Allah, the Lord of majesty and honor,\nمِنْ جَمِيْعِ الذُّنُوْبِ وَالْآثَامِ\nMIN JAMEE-I’Z ZONOOBE WAL AASAAME\nto forgive my all sins and offenses.\nEach night in Rajab, repeat 1,000 times:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAH.\nThere is no deity except Allah.",
    "Fasting, Prayers & Tawhid\nFast on Thursday, Friday and Saturday in Rajab.\nIn Rajab, recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 100, 1,000 or 10,000 times. On Fridays in Rajab, recite it 100 times.\nOn one night in Rajab, recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 100 times.\nOn a day you fast in Rajab, offer a four-unit prayer: in the first unit recite [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) 100 times, and in the second [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 200 times.\nOn a Friday in Rajab, between the obligatory Zuhr and Asr prayers, offer a four-unit prayer: in each unit recite [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once, [Ayat al-Kursi](A4) 7 times and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 5 times. Then repeat 10 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللهَ الَّذِيْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ وَاَسْاَلُهُ التَّوْبَةَ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA WA ASALOHUT TAWBAH.\nI seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no deity except Him, and I ask Him for repentance.\nOn one night in Rajab, offer a ten-unit prayer, reciting in each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) three times.",
    "Sixty-Unit Prayer & Dua\nOffer a sixty-unit prayer in Rajab.\nEach night, offer two units of this prayer in the first unit of which [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) is recited once, [Surah al-Kafirun](A113) (No. 109) repeated three times, and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) recited one time.\nAfter the two units, raise your hands toward the sky and say:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU,\nThere is no god save Allah, the One and Only Who has no partner.\nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ\nLAHUL MULKO WA LAHUL HAMDO, \nTo Him is the kingdom and to Him is all praise.\nيُحْيِيْ وَيُمِيْتُ وَهُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ\nYOHYEE WA YOMEETO WA HOWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTO \nHe restores to live and cause to die and He is Ever-living and He never dies.\nبِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nBEYADEHIL KHAYRO WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEERUN \nIn His Hands is all goodness, He has power over all things,\nوَاِلَيْهِ الْمَصِيْرُ\nWA ELAYHIL MASEERO, \nand to Him is the return of all things.\nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEME, \nThere is neither might nor strength save with Allah, the Most High, the All-great.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ النَّبِيِّ الْاُمِّيِّ وَاٰلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADENIN NABIYYIL UMMIYYE WA AALEHI.\nO Allah, (please do) bless Muhammad, the Ummi Prophet, and his Household.\nPass your hand over your face while uttering the last statement.",
    "Daily Litanies, Rajab to Ramazan\nIn Rajab, Sha’ban and Ramazan, every day and every night, recite each of these 3 times: [Surah al-Faatehah](A5), Ayah al-Kursi, [Surah al-Kafirun](A113), [Surah al-Tawheed](A116), [Surah al-Falaq](A117), [Surah al-Naas](A118), and this litany:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAAHE, WAL HAMDO LILLAAHE \nAll glory be to Allah; all praise be to Allah;\nوَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nWA LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAL LAAHO AKBARO, \nthere is no god save Allah; Allah is the Greatest; \nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A’LIYYIL A’ZEEM.\nand there is no might and no strength save with Allah, the High, the Magnificent.\nAlso recite 3 times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMDIN.\nO Allah bless Muhammad and his family\nAlso recite 3 times:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LIL MOAMENEENA WAL MOAMENAAT.\nAllah please forgive the believing men & women\nAlso recite 400 times:\nاَسْتَغْفِرُ اللّٰهَ وَاَتُوْبُ اِلَيْهِ\nASTAGHFERUL LAAHA WA ATOOBO ELAYHE.\nI seek forgiveness from Allah, and I turn to Him in repentance."
